#set par(first-line-indent: 0em)

Shared, high-level vocabularies make enforcing privacy and security policies in applications tractable, even at real-world scale and complexity.

// Enforcing Privacy and Security policies in real-world applications is tractable when enforceemnt engine and users agree on a shared, high-level vocabulary of effects.

#v(2em)

There are many techniques for ensuring that programs are compliant with privacy
and security requirement. However, while the concerns are paramount, reliable
techniques are used only in ultra-high danger domains. This is because such
techniques are either inefficient or highly unwieldy to use. In this thesis I
explore an approach that uses high-level vocabularies that makes sophisticated
safeguards accessible to users and developers by meeting them where they are at.
At the same time, this vocabulary maps efficiently to sound enforcement techniques.

